---
import '../styles/global.css';
import NavigationBar from '../components/NavigationBar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { Font } from 'astro:assets';
---
<style>
section {
  min-height: 100svh;
  max-width: 80vw;
  margin: 0 auto;
  font-family: var(--font-inconsolata);
}

span {
  font-weight: bold;
}

li {
  margin: 16px 0;
  font-weight: normal;
}
</style>

<html lang="en">
	<head>
    <Font cssVariable='--font-inconsolata' />
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/ico" href="/favicon.ico" />
		<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <meta name="description" content="A page full of all of my daily gadgets!" />
    <title>uses - developing with DominickCS_</title>
	</head>
	<body>
    <NavigationBar />
    <main>
      <section>
        <div>
          <h2>Hardware</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><span>HP Elitebook 850 G8</span> - Intel i5 1145G7 / 32GB DDR4 RAM | NixOS | daily driver</li>
            <li><span>My Battle Station</span> - AMD Ryzen 7 3700X / GTX 1080 Ti / 64GB DDR4 RAM | NixOS | still runs minecraft like a champ</li>
            <li><span>Raspberry Pi 3b</span> - barely use this thing, want to get something built on it soon.</li>
            <li><span>Arduino Uno r3</span> - yeah, just yeah....</li>
            <li><span>Flipper Zero</span> - Unleashed Firmware | Wish I used this more</li>
            <li><span>Logitech G-Pro Wireless</span> - clicks three times when you click once, otherwise good</li>
            <li><span>Logitech G502 Hero</span> - (war veteran) on second set of mouse switches, sits pretty on my desk @ work</li>
            <li><span>Keychron C1</span> - nice knock, just keep away from the office, or basically anywhere quiet</li>
            <li><span>Glorius GMMK 60%</span> - heavier than my workstation, love it so much though, will never let you go</li>
            <li><span>AKG P120</span> - makes me sound smooth like butter</li>
            <li><span>Logitech C920s</span> - webcam so i can see myself ramble about things</li>
            <li><span>Sony WHCH720N Wireless Headphones</span> - nice lightweight over-the-ear noise-cancelling budget-friendly pair</li>
            <li><span>Canon G7x mk III</span> - watched one review video, instantly purchased</li>
            <li><span>iPhone 13 Pro</span> - wish Google didn't hate their userbase, forced to use iPhone</li>
            <li><span>Audio Technica ATH-M50x Headphones</span> - used when I make music, ol' reliable </li>
            <li><span>Secretlab Titan XL Chair</span> - not gonna lie, never had a chair not break on me before, been super reliable</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>OS & Desktop</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><span>NixOS</span> - I am really into reproducible builds as of lately.</li>
            <li><span>Sway on Wayland</span> - love it </li>
            <li><span>PipeWire</span> - it makes me feel like I know what I am doing</li>
            <li><span>Catppuccin Frape Theme</span> - i am not a good ricer, soooo</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>Editor & Terminal</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><span>Neovim w/ LazyVim</span> - equally the hardest, and best decision i've made in my linux career</li>
            <li><span>Zsh w/ Oh-My-Zsh</span> - i don't like typing cd lol</li>
            <li><span>Kitty</span> - it's gud</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>Dev Stack</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><span>Java / Spring Framework</span> - learned it in college, kinda goated</li>
            <li><span>Rust</span> - learning currently</li>
            <li><span>C</span> - pulling out what little hair i currently have learning this :D</li>
            <li><span>Javascript</span> - this and many of the frameworks, still need to get familiar with angular</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>Music Production</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><span>FL Studio DAW</span> - cracked since FL 8 in 2011, finally bought legit in 2024 LOL</li>
            <li><span>Arturia Keylab 61 mk iii</span> - fancy; still don't know music theory though...</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
	</body>
    <Footer />
</html>
